error[E0277]: capability set widening: this handler's method declares `(FsRead,)`, so it may mint only `Client<(FsRead,)>` — `(FsWrite,)` is a different capability set
  --> tests/ui/widened_capability_set.rs:33:33
   |
33 |         let client = input.turn.client::<(FsWrite,)>();
   |                                 ^^^^^^ `(FsWrite,)` is not the declared set `(FsRead,)`
   |
   = help: the trait `Declares<(FsWrite,)>` is not implemented for `(FsRead,)`
   = note: a handler may use exactly the set its method declares. Write `turn.client()` and let the declared set be inferred; to use another capability, add it to the method's `Client<..>` declaration so the runtime's pre-flight check can verify the peer serves it (PLX-102).
note: required by a bound in `Turn::<C>::client`
  --> src/runtime/declared.rs
   |
   |     pub fn client<D>(&self) -> Client<D>
   |            ------ required by a bound in this associated function
...
   |         C: Declares<D>,
   |            ^^^^^^^^^^^ required by this bound in `Turn::<C>::client`
